<div class="wrap">
  <header class="top">
    <h1>Overnight Run, 13 October</h1>
    <p class="deck">Whether the night met your goal for the record, what it did, what waits for your review, and what it cost.</p>
    <p class="stamp">13 Oct 2026, 20:40 UTC (22:40 yours) · sizes at b67abe3d2</p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-answer">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="h-answer">The answer</h2>
      <button class="select" type="button" data-target="s-answer" aria-label="Select the text of this section">Select</button>
    </div>
    <div class="speak" id="s-answer">
      <p class="pt">Yes. FACTS and POSITIONS together went from 360.6K characters to 124.1K, 66% smaller. The target was at most about 145K.</p>
      <p class="pt">The three skills that took in the rules that left grew by 7.8K. Counted with that growth, it's still about 132K.</p>
      <p class="pt">The record test got no worse. The finished record scored 30 of 30. The bar was the first run's 27, and the old record scored 28 in the same grading.</p>
      <p class="pt">What the coordinator reads at every boot went from 616K characters to 362K. That's roughly 230K tokens of context down to about 135K.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Sources</h3>
      <p><b>1.</b> <code>wc -m</code> on <code>FACTS.md</code> and <code>POSITIONS.md</code> at <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/715641924">715641924</a>, the numbering base before tonight's work, and at <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/b67abe3d2">b67abe3d2</a>, the last removal. The target: your words of 17:23 UTC and the measure, in the <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/coordinator/BOOT.md">boot note</a>.</p>
      <p><b>2.</b> &ldquo;Sizes&rdquo;, point 2: 124.1K plus 7.8K is 131.9K.</p>
      <p><b>3.</b> &ldquo;The record test&rdquo;, points 2 to 4.</p>
      <p><b>4.</b> &ldquo;Sizes&rdquo;, point 4.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

----
  <section aria-labelledby="h-review">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="h-review">For your review</h2>
      <button class="select" type="button" data-target="s-review" aria-label="Select the text of this section">Select</button>
    </div>
    <div class="speak" id="s-review">
      <p>These are the choices taken at their defaults while you were away, and the points the workers raised. Nothing here holds the work. Each one says what landed, then the other way.</p>

      <h3>The record's form</h3>
      <p class="pt">The history files were rebuilt, as you said at 17:01 UTC (19:01 yours). Each change there keeps the entry's earlier line, which costs only disk. The other way: keep only where a change came from, and get the old text from git.</p>
      <p class="pt">Each entry's number is its line before tonight's work, so the numbers have gaps but match the drafts and the test. A pointer to another entry is the number alone, and former titles are kept, so an old note that cites a title still finds its entry. The other ways: numbers from 1, pointers that carry title words, and no former titles.</p>
      <p class="pt">The pilot's record test had one reader, graded against the first run's answers from the old record. The other way: the kit's full run, two fresh readers graded blind side by side.</p>
      <p class="pt">When a decision and a fact tell the same thing, POSITIONS holds the decision and FACTS the state, each pointing to the other by number. A script flags each entry over 0.6K. The other way: a reader's check alone.</p>

      <h3>What left FACTS and POSITIONS, and what stayed</h3>
      <p class="pt">Your decisions on how the coordinator works with you left POSITIONS at the end, for the history, each with its new home in a skill named. Your words for them are in the history now. The other way, the plan's first default: keep them in POSITIONS, your words there and the rule in the skill.</p>
      <p class="pt">The facts about the container and the platform left FACTS for the skills, each by its home. Only the fact about the shell setup script for the gate's runners stays. Three of your decisions on the test suites and the gate stay in POSITIONS, one whole and two in part, because that's where your decisions live. The other way: keep the container facts in FACTS.</p>

      <h3>The coordinator skill</h3>
      <p class="pt">It's a core that's always loaded, now 15K against a target of about 10K, and six parts. All five rules that no search of past failures covered were kept. The four with no failure found were dropped, one folded into the rule to search the record first. The other way for the core: move its rules on pages into a part, about 1.2K less.</p>
      <p class="pt">The git-check hook is the platform's hook that asks for a commit after every turn. After a process stop, the coordinator tells you it's back, and only you can turn it off, by switching to manual mode. At 15:42 UTC (17:42 yours) you'd asked for the coordinator to reset it at each restart. The platform's permission check refused that way, so the check against the rules to keep called this a change of meaning. The other way: the coordinator tries, and asks you only if it's refused.</p>
      <p class="pt">The review list's one home is PLAN, under each batch, and the review queue file only sorts it. The other way: the queue file as the home, read at every boot.</p>
      <p class="pt">The batch part says the commit stage's record pass gets the record part quoted in its prompt. The batch script doesn't do that today. The other ways: make quoting it a step of preparing a batch, or change the line to say what the script does.</p>
      <p class="pt">The held list went from 22.7K to 8.4K. The points that the new skill holds, and the done or settled ones, were closed, and the commit's message names each. The outline review had asked that nothing leave the list before you'd seen it. The other way: keep them until you've read the list.</p>

      <h3>The other two skills</h3>
...

      <h3>Next, and owed</h3>
      <p class="pt">INDEX's form. It stayed as it was, read whole at every boot, as you kept it on 30 September. It's now the largest boot read, 200K, 55% of it. The other way: group its lines by topic, for about 0.5M to 1M tokens written, an estimate.</p>
      <p class="pt">Owed and found: the gap-ledger tool's tests, where 10 of 13 fail on the current code because their expectations are stale, and four history notes that name cloud-container's old headings.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Sources</h3>
      <p><b>1.</b> <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/coordinator/process-engineering/record-store-review.md">record-store-review.md</a>, section 5, items 1, 2 and 6. Your word of 17:01 UTC: the boot note and HELD.</p>
      <p><b>2.</b> Same section, items 3, 4, 5 and 7. The former titles cost 70K bytes once.</p>
      <p><b>3.</b> Same section, item 8.</p>
      <p><b>4.</b> <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/coordinator/process-engineering/coordinator-writer-task.md">coordinator-writer-task.md</a>, section 4, decisions 2 and 4.</p>
      <p><b>5.</b> Writer's task, decision 17; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/coordinator/process-engineering/coordinator-skill-outline-review.md">coordinator-skill-outline-review.md</a>, section 4.2, decision 17; the plan's first default: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/coordinator/process-engineering/coordinator-rewrite-plan.md">coordinator-rewrite-plan.md</a>, section 4, decision 17.</p>
      <p><b>6.</b> Writer's task, decision 23 and &ldquo;The review's own&rdquo;; outline review, section 4.2, decision 23 and &ldquo;New, from this review&rdquo;. The fact that stays: F-203, <code>explorations/experiment/env.sh</code>. The three decisions: P-39 whole, P-102 and P-103 in part.</p>
      <p><b>7.</b> Writer's task, decisions 6, 7 and 8. The core: <code>SKILL.md</code> 14,984 at b67abe3d2; the skill writer's first report, decision not taken 1 (the core was 13.2K then).</p>
      <p><b>8.</b> The kept-list check, M3; the skill writer's first report, decision not taken 3; writer's task, decision 24; your point of 15:42 UTC, still on HELD as &ldquo;the hook reset as changed&rdquo;. The skill's text: <code>SKILL.md</code>, &ldquo;The boot&rdquo;, last bullet.</p>
      <p><b>9.</b> The skill writer's second report, decisions not taken; the boot note, &ldquo;For the morning page&rdquo;.</p>
      <p><b>10.</b> Same. The line: the coordinator skill's <code>references/batch.md</code>.</p>
      <p><b>11.</b> Commit <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/0528e963b">0528e963b</a> and its message; outline review, section 5, item 5. HELD.md: 22,657 at 715641924, 8,363 now.</p>
      <p><b>12.</b> Outline review, section 4.2, decision 22; the rewrite plan, section 4, decision 22 (the email rule). Commit <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/4c11b10c3">4c11b10c3</a>: fortress-repo's <code>references/committing.md</code>, <code>records.md</code> &ldquo;The repository's history&rdquo;, and <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/.claude/skills/fortress-repo/references/gate.md">gate.md</a> &ldquo;Comparing with an earlier run&rdquo;. The masks: the skill writer's third report, &ldquo;Where the task's reasons were wrong&rdquo;.</p>
      <p><b>13.</b> The third report, decisions not taken; reworded in <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/8ca0d7e61">8ca0d7e61</a>.</p>
      <p><b>14.</b> The third report, decisions not taken; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/.claude/skills/cloud-container/references/stops.md">stops.md</a>, &ldquo;The weekly usage limit&rdquo;; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/.claude/skills/cloud-container/SKILL.md">cloud-container's SKILL.md</a>, its description.</p>
      <p><b>15.</b> The third report (the two registrations) and the fourth (cold-read flags 49 and 50, the wait); <code>stops.md</code>, line 64; <code>hooks.md</code>, &ldquo;The transcript backup&rdquo;.</p>
      <p><b>16.</b> The boot note, &ldquo;For the morning page, from the chunk writers&rdquo;: P-26 and P-8. Their full texts: <code>facts-extract.sh 'history:P-26'</code> and <code>'history:P-8'</code>.</p>
      <p><b>17.</b> Same: P-43, P-7 and P-25. P-7's copy: F-164 (the text's last edit is of 2010-12-09, the copy of 2011-02-02).</p>
      <p><b>18.</b> Same: ledger rows 400 (&ldquo;closed&rdquo; in old P-40), 473 (fixed), 577 (maybe closable) and 642 (contested only by the tool); F-62 with F-72, and F-67 with F-68; F-48's two defects and F-36's latent <code>boundsFor</code> defect; F-98's reading of <code>generalTestFailed</code>. Also live files that quote old FACTS titles, which the title fallback resolves.</p>
      <p><b>19.</b> <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/coordinator/process-engineering/coordinator-rewrite-plan.md">coordinator-rewrite-plan.md</a>, section 4, decision 3; writer's task, decision 3. The trial boot read INDEX whole, about 74K tokens, its largest read.</p>
      <p><b>20.</b> <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/coordinator/tools/test_ledger.py">tools/test_ledger.py</a>; the boot note, &ldquo;Owed after the consolidation&rdquo; and &ldquo;For the morning page&rdquo;.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-cost">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="h-cost">The cost</h2>
      <button class="select" type="button" data-target="s-cost" aria-label="Select the text of this section">Select</button>
    </div>
    <div class="speak" id="s-cost">
      <p class="pt">Tokens written are input plus cache writes. Cached reads are left out, as you ask. From 14:40 to 20:33 UTC (16:40 to 22:33 yours), before this page was written, the work wrote about 11.5M.</p>
      <p class="pt">The split: the workers about 9.7M; the headless skill writers, separate Claude sessions run from the command line, 0.6M; and the coordinating session 1.1M.</p>
      <p class="pt">The window starts before your approval at 17:13 UTC (19:13 yours), so it also holds the record store's design and the skill's outline, both written before it. And each transcript touched since 14:40 counts whole, so a little of it is older still.</p>
      <p class="pt">For scale, a climb batch, one batch of rungs on the compiled path, writes 5M to 7M.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Sources</h3>
      <p><b>1.</b> <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/coordinator/tools/spend.py">tools/spend.py</a> over the session's agent transcripts, read by the coordinator at 20:33 UTC. The boot note's figure at 20:10 UTC was 10.9M.</p>
      <p><b>2.</b> The same count. Each part is rounded, so they sum to 11.4M.</p>
      <p><b>3.</b> The design: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/92827fca8">92827fca8</a>, 16:30 UTC. The outline: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/commit/d84be672f">d84be672f</a>, 16:38 UTC.</p>
      <p><b>4.</b> For example, batch 10 wrote 6.26M: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/main/explorations/coordinator/process-engineering/batch-redesign.md">batch-redesign.md</a>, line 21.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

